{"schema":2,"commit":"444732438d3bc0a956d1902b3ef62ca92055dbf0","branch":"feat/window-close-and-ota","base_sha":"07d76700e0726096a6a911ab207c26cd9aaceaa3","message":"feat: close all windows when parked and a door opens\n\nPorts WinClose's SWI69 window control as an opt-in foreground service that is\nindependent of ABRP: no token, no GPS, no upload cadence. The driver opening a\ndoor while the car is in P at a readable 0 km/h pulses UP at all four areas for\nfive seconds, then STOP.\n\nOnly the parts that serve that one behaviour are taken. WinClose's speed and\ntime arming, configurable delay, warning beep, per-window modes and position\nreads are all absent — the target car is a Comfort trim whose motors carry no\nposition sensor, so a close can be neither verified nor cancelled.\n\nThe pulse, the door edge detector and the eligibility policy are pure classes\nwith unit tests. STOP is attempted from a finally block on every exit, including\nan interrupted sleep, a refused write and a sender that throws, because a pulse\nthat stops arriving leaves the motors wherever they were.\n\nGuards worth naming, several of them learned from reading WinClose rather than\nfrom the port itself:\n\n- A wake lock spans the pulse. This fires as the driver leaves, which is exactly\n  when the head unit suspends; without it the glass can stop halfway with no\n  STOP sent.\n- A fresh listener registration replays the door's current state. That replay\n  seeds the edge detector instead of triggering it, or a binder reconnect while\n  the door stands open would close the windows on someone halfway out.\n- WinClose's 60-second cooldown, so reaching back into the car does not run a\n  second pulse.\n- The service stops itself on a non-SWI69 generation, and the switch is disabled\n  unless the process holds system uid — only the unstable flavor declares\n  android.uid.system, so a stable build could otherwise offer a toggle whose\n  every command would fail.\n\nThis is the project's first write to the vehicle. README, SECURITY, AGENTS,\nCONTRIBUTING and DISCLAIMER all claimed the app never writes; that claim is\nretracted and scoped rather than quietly left standing.\n\nUntested on a car. The feature is off by default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","coding_time_nanos":650623902000,"totals":{"added_lines":937,"ai_added_lines":937,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":9,"ai_deleted_lines":2,"human_deleted_lines":7,"files":18,"tokens":{"input":111,"output":35775,"cache_read":15602271,"cache_write":120867},"models":{"claude-opus-5":937}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":937,"deleted_lines":2,"suggested_lines":5493,"accepted_lines":937,"tokens":{"input":111,"output":35775,"cache_read":15602271,"cache_write":120867}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":939,"completion":0,"human":7},"files":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":8,"deleted_lines":3,"ai_added_lines":8,"human_deleted_lines":3,"lines":[{"start":18,"end":18,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":18,"end":18,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":19,"end":19,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":19,"end":19,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":20,"end":20,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":20,"end":20,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":21,"end":22,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":46,"end":48,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"}]},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":3,"deleted_lines":2,"ai_added_lines":3,"human_deleted_lines":2,"lines":[{"start":7,"end":7,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":7,"end":7,"type":"delete","author_type